<title>FRANCE: France sees U.N. approving more wheat for Iraq.</title>
<headline>France sees U.N. approving more wheat for Iraq.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>France, which received a U.N. go-ahead last week to ship 100,000 tonnes of wheat to Iraq, expects clearance for a further 200,000 tonnes in coming weeks, a French diplomatic source said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The 200,000 tonnes cover two separate contracts for 100,000 tonnes of French wheat that exporters sold to Iraq in December under a U.N.-monitored oil-for-food agreement.</p>
<p>U.N. approval of the two sales would complete the clearance process for the first wave of French wheat sales to Iraq --</p>
</text>
